.TH TAGPLAY 1 "2026-11-02" "tagplay 0.9" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tagplay \- query-driven terminal music player with analog-media DSP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tagplay
.RI [ options ]
.IR MUSIC_DIR ...
.br
.B tagplay
.B \-q
.I EXPR
.RB [ \-s
.IR FIELDS ]
.RB [ \-t ]
.IR MUSIC_DIR ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tagplay
scans the given directories for FLAC, MP3 and WAV files, reads their
tags into a cache, and presents an fzf-style incremental search over
the whole library: the match count collapses as you type, and
.B Enter
plays the result.
Playback runs through the audiotard DSP chain (tube, tape, vinyl,
shellac-78 and AM-radio emulations, a ten-band EQ and shelving tone
controls), with a live spectrum trace available in the terminal.
Internet radio stations ride along in the same queue.
.PP
The first scan of a large library takes a while; subsequent runs
re-read only files whose size or mtime changed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-q " EXPR"
One-shot mode: print the paths matching the query expression and
exit.  Suitable for scripting and piping.
.TP
.BI \-s " FIELDS"
Sort specification for
.BR \-q ,
a comma-separated field list; a leading
.B \-
means descending (e.g.\&
.BR year,album,track " or " \-year,title ).
.TP
.B \-t
With
.BR \-q :
print artist/title/album/length columns instead of bare paths.
.TP
.BI \-C " PATH"
Use
.I PATH
as the tag cache (default
.IR ~/.cache/tagplay/cache.bin ).
.TP
.B \-n
No cache: scan fresh and do not write a cache.
.TP
.BI \-D " FILE"
Debug: decode
.I FILE
fully, print rate, channels, duration, peak and a seek test, exit.
.TP
.BI \-T " FILE"
Debug: dump
.IR FILE 's
tags (escaped), format and duration, exit.
.SH QUERY LANGUAGE
The same expressions work interactively, in
.BR \-q ,
and in
.BR tagplay-gui (1).
.TP
.I bare words
Substring match on any field; several words are an implicit AND.
.TP
.BI field " = " value
Exact match, case-insensitive;
.B !=
negates.
.TP
.BI field " ~ \(dq" regex \(dq
PCRE2 regular expression, case-insensitive.
.TP
.BR year<1990 ", " length>=3:00 ", " rate=96000
Numeric comparisons
.RB ( < " " <= " " > " " >= " " = " " != ).
.TP
.B & | ! ( )
Boolean operators;
.B ,
is a synonym for
.BR & .
.PP
Fields: any tag key present in the library, plus the pseudo-fields
.BR path ", " format ", " length ", " rate ", " year ", " track ", "
.BR disc .
Use the
.B t
key on a cursored track to see exactly which fields it carries.
.SH VIEWS AND KEYS
.B Tab
cycles query \(-> list \(-> queue \(-> query.
.TP
.B query view
Type to filter;
.B Enter
plays the matches (replacing the queue);
.B Ctrl-U
clears the line;
.B :
starts a command.
.TP
.B list view
.BR j / k /arrows
move;
.B Space
toggles the
.B [x]
selection mark;
.B a
selects all shown;
.B i
inverts;
.B c
clears;
.B Enter
plays the selection (consuming it) or, with nothing marked, the
matches;
.B t
shows every tag on the cursored track.
.TP
.B queue view
Shows what is playing:
.BR j / k
move,
.B Enter
jumps,
.B Space
pauses,
.BR left / right
seek 10 s,
.BR < / >
seek 60 s,
.B r
restarts the track,
.B s
stops,
.BR J / K
reorder the queue,
.B t
inspects tags,
.B a
shows embedded art.
.SH COMMANDS
Every
.B :
command works identically here and in
.BR tagplay-gui (1).
.SS Search and curation
.TP
.B :sel
Show only the marked tracks, in playlist order, for editing
.RB ( Space
unmarks); any typing returns to normal search.
.TP
.BI :sort " f1,-f2"
Sort matches; leading
.B \-
descending; bare
.B :sort
clears.
.TP
.BI :group " KEY"
Group matches under dim headers (any tag key;
.B :group off
clears).
.TP
.BI :cols " +year -album"
Toggle row fields (album year genre fmt dur track); persists in
.IR ~/.config/tagplay/config .
.SS Playlists
.TP
.BI :save " NAME\fR, \fP" :load " NAME\fR, \fP" :lists "\fR, \fP" :clear
Plain
.B .m3u
files under
.IR ~/.config/tagplay/playlists/ .
.B :save
keeps the selection (or, with none, the matches);
.B :load
loads into the selection.
.SS Transport
.TP
.BR :p ", " :n ", " :b ", " :stop
Pause/resume, next, previous, stop (queue kept).
.B Ctrl-P/N/B
do the same without clearing the query.
.TP
.BI :seek " 1:23"
Absolute seek in the current track.
.TP
.BR :vol " 80, " :vol " +5, " :vol " \-5"
Volume, absolute or relative percent.
.SS Audiotard DSP
.TP
.BI ":dsp " "tube\fR|\fPtape\fR|\fPvinyl\fR|\fPshellac\fR|\fPam AMOUNT"
Character modes; amount 0..1 (0.5 = the calibrated preset).  For
.B am
the amount is a day\(->night morph: 1.0 is night-time skywave DX with
deep selective fades and the adjacent channel's heterodyne whistle.
.TP
.BI :dsp " eq G1..G10"
Ten ISO octave bands, dB (\-18..+18).
.TP
.BI :dsp " bt BASS TREBLE"
Shelving tone controls, dB (\-12..+12).
.TP
.B :dsp off
Bypass (crossfaded; mode changes never pop).
.TP
.BI :dsp " set NAME VALUE"
Any granular parameter of the current mode; see
.B :dsp show
for names, units and ranges.
.TP
.BR ":dsp params" ", " ":dsp meas" ", " ":dsp show"
One-line parameter dump; THD/H2/H3/noise/SNR measurement on a shadow
chain; full parameter-and-measurement page.
.SS Spectrum (terminal)
.TP
.B :fft
Toggle the braille spectrum trace under the status area: clean
signal dim, processed signal bright \(em the same analyzer as the
GUI.
.B :fft ema A
sets exponential averaging (0 raw .. 1 slow);
.B :fft avgn N
a plain mean over the last N frames (2..64);
.BR ":fft on" / off
explicit.
.SS Radio and misc
.TP
.BI ":radio add " "URL NAME\fR, \fP" ":radio rm " NAME
Manage stations
.RI ( ~/.config/tagplay/stations ,
one \(dqurl TAB name\(dq per line; a starter set is seeded on first
run).
.TP
.BR :ls ", " :stats ", " :help ", " :q
List matches; tag-key frequency; built-in help; quit.
.SH DSP NOTES
Effects render in a block pipeline with cosine crossfades at every
seam: mode switches, parameter drags, and the off\(<->effect
boundary are all click-free, and each mode is loudness-matched to
the clean signal by a measured RMS gain.  All filter corners are
clamped below Nyquist, so low-rate material (22.05 kHz and below)
stays finite.  If the audio device refuses a sample rate, playback
continues silently but says so loudly in the message line and
retries on the next track.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.cache/tagplay/cache.bin
Tag cache (versioned; rebuilds automatically on format change).
.TP
.I ~/.cache/tagplay/stderr.log
Library chatter, kept off the screen.
.TP
.I ~/.config/tagplay/playlists/*.m3u
Saved playlists (portable).
.TP
.I ~/.config/tagplay/stations
Radio stations, \(dqurl TAB name\(dq per line.
.TP
.I ~/.config/tagplay/config
Persisted display settings
.RB ( :cols ).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR XDG_CACHE_HOME ", " XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Relocate the directories above.
.SH EXAMPLES
Everything from 96 kHz FLACs, grouped by album:
.PP
.nf
    tagplay ~/music
    rate=96000
    :group album
.fi
.PP
All pre-1800 FLAC tracks as a sorted table, for a script:
.PP
.nf
    tagplay \-q 'year<1800 & format=flac' \-s year,album,track \-t ~/music
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tagplay-gui (1),
.BR tagview (1)
.PP
Source and README:
